#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100894 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100732 :question/id #uuid "891e9004-961b-539a-ab93-0752347fd077" :question/math-academy-id "e-541" :question/problem "Find the particular solution to the differential equation $\\cos(3y)\\dfrac {\\textrm{d}y} {\\textrm{d}x} + \\sin(2x) = 0$ given that  $y\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{4}\\right) = 0.$ Assume that $-\\dfrac{\\pi}{6} < y < \\dfrac{\\pi}{6} .$" :question/worked-solution "We first find the general solution, and then apply the given initial condition to find a particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3y)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x) \\\\ \\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡(3y)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =-\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡(3y)\\,\\text{d}y & =-\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3y) & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)+C \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(3y) & =\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)+{C}_{1}\\,,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C_1=3C.$\n\nNow let's apply the condition $y\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{4}\\right) = 0$ to find $C_1\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(\\frac{\\pi }{4}) & =0 \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\cdot 0) & =\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{4})+{C}_{1} \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(0) & =\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})+{C}_{1} \\\\ 0 & =0+{C}_{1} \\\\ {C}_{1} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we get the particular solution in implicit form:\n\n$$\n\\sin(3y)   =  \\dfrac {3} {2} \\cos(2x)\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "de2e3a7c-d4f0-5b0f-8014-1519fb3a9473" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101297 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "00ad7b38-011b-5bbc-ad6f-119764a28f5c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{4x}-\\frac{1}{4})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284794} {:answer/id #uuid "5cd60163-91c2-5f68-b12b-44f98e6c673c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{4x}+5)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285640} {:answer/id #uuid "60978d4b-4f9a-549a-a78c-7b2ab10d8ff1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{{e}^{4x}}{4}+C)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285674} {:answer/id #uuid "675c44fb-e5b5-5cc4-a665-61ee54152b6a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{{e}^{4x}+4{e}^{5}-1}{4})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285732} {:answer/id #uuid "dd44c23d-4f4e-5432-b33e-dff52c07b119" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{{e}^{4x}}{4}+{e}^{5}+\\frac{1}{4})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286799}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "675c44fb-e5b5-5cc4-a665-61ee54152b6a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{{e}^{4x}+4{e}^{5}-1}{4})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285732} :answer-field/id #uuid "af959d06-569d-5cc3-8e3f-fadee181c763" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287510}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e844aafc-6198-5e85-8b96-36f86924e412" :question/math-academy-id "q-20071" :question/problem "Find the particular solution to the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={e}^{4x-y}$ that satisfies $y(0)=5.$" :question/worked-solution "We first find the general solution and then apply the given initial condition to find a particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={e}^{4x-y} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={e}^{4x}\\cdot {e}^{-y} \\\\ {e}^{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={e}^{4x} \\\\ \\int {e}^{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {e}^{4x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int {e}^{y}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int {e}^{4x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ {e}^{y} & =\\frac{{e}^{4x}}{4}+C\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the natural logarithm to both sides, we find the general solution:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{y}) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{{e}^{4x}}{4}+C) \\\\ y & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{{e}^{4x}}{4}+C)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now apply the condition $y(0)=5$ to find $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(0) & =5 \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{{e}^{4\\cdot 0}}{4}+C) & =5 \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{1}{4}+C) & =5 \\\\ \\frac{1}{4}+C & ={e}^{5} \\\\ C & =\\frac{4{e}^{5}-1}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus the particular solution of $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={e}^{4x-y}$ that satisfies the condition $y(0)=5$ is\n\n$$\ny=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{{e}^{4x}+4{e}^{5}-1}{4}).\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101539 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "289b6d64-a211-5da5-9a4e-e626db7e48e1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{4{e}^{x}}{x+2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345715} {:answer/id #uuid "539c1b15-7731-56bd-9c2a-ca623649b96c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{{e}^{x+1}}{x+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346061} {:answer/id #uuid "5e3ba5d5-d097-5032-a55f-f8306cff701c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{2{e}^{x}}{x+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346163} {:answer/id #uuid "9cfbb45a-ec8c-5ace-9f06-4292bd88e210" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{2{e}^{-x}}{{x}^{2}+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346719} {:answer/id #uuid "adf0d1d2-3ce8-5813-906f-ee26fca0599b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{4{e}^{-x}}{{x}^{2}+2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346869}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5e3ba5d5-d097-5032-a55f-f8306cff701c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{2{e}^{x}}{x+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346163} :answer-field/id #uuid "2c1ace9b-199b-55d1-97e0-bde3eb07a2d4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347675}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "167e1aa1-119e-56a2-b6bf-0adbf44240f8" :question/math-academy-id "q-79372" :question/problem "Find the particular solution to the differential equation $(\\frac{1}{xy}+\\frac{1}{y})\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=1$ that satisfies $y(1)=e.$" :question/worked-solution "We first find the general solution and then apply the given initial condition to find a particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\frac{1}{xy}+\\frac{1}{y})\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}(\\frac{1+x}{x})\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{x}{x+1} \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{x}{x+1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int (1-\\frac{1}{x+1})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|y| & =x-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+1|+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the natural logarithm to both sides, we find the general solution:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|} & ={e}^{x-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+1|+C} \\\\ |y| & ={e}^{x-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+1|+C} \\\\ |y| & ={e}^{x}\\cdot {e}^{-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+1|}\\cdot {e}^{C} \\\\ y & =\\frac{K{e}^{x}}{x+1},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K=\\pm {e}^{C}$ is an arbitrary constant. \n\nWe now apply the initial condition $y(1)=e$ to find $K:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(1) & =e \\\\ \\frac{K{e}^{1}}{1+1} & =e \\\\ K & =2\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus the particular solution of $(\\frac{1}{xy}+\\frac{1}{y})\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=1$ that satisfies the condition $y(1)=e$ is\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{2{e}^{x}}{x+1}\\,.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235352 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d913ad1f-de16-5603-834b-341786551f9a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2/({x}^{2}-2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234884}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d913ad1f-de16-5603-834b-341786551f9a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2/({x}^{2}-2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234884} :answer-field/id #uuid "b3011aa0-ebf7-5b93-b9a2-848f373cb2d6" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186235190}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "93ff4d9b-f05d-54cb-bfec-91c45b5200dc" :question/math-academy-id "q-128192" :question/problem "Find the solution to the initial value problem \n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=x{y}^{2},\\,y(1)=2.\n$$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $y(x)=\\,\\,$ \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "From part 6, we found the general solution\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-2{({x}^{2}+K)}^{-1},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K$ is an arbitrary constant.\n\nNow, we apply the initial condition $y(1)=2$ to find $K:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(1) & =2 \\\\ -2{({1}^{2}+K)}^{-1} & =2 \\\\ 1+K & =-1 \\\\ K & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to our initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny=-2({x}^{2}-2)^{-1}=-\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}-2}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186240790 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "158257b0-40d3-5bb7-bac5-6e36056355d0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|-y=2{x}^{2}-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238234} {:answer/id #uuid "16004206-d689-5265-94c9-1376fc2a7419" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|={x}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238241} {:answer/id #uuid "41e7778c-2d5c-54b6-9c23-07562072de44" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|+y=2{x}^{2}+2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238628} {:answer/id #uuid "77b24ff7-d9d9-52ef-a8e8-e1a351aed83f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|-y={x}^{2}-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239088} {:answer/id #uuid "dd57c394-1382-5901-b867-e989f439cece" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|+y={x}^{2}+2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239988}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "77b24ff7-d9d9-52ef-a8e8-e1a351aed83f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|-y={x}^{2}-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239088} :answer-field/id #uuid "30ba2846-d824-5e4c-aa9d-3131e60267bf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240419}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "cf490795-4587-5d21-a17e-b28b1511e0a5" :question/math-academy-id "q-104058" :question/problem "Find the particular solution to the differential equation $(\\frac{1}{xy}-\\frac{1}{x})\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=2$ that satisfies $y(1)=1.$" :question/worked-solution "We first find the general solution and then apply the given initial condition to find a particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\frac{1}{xy}-\\frac{1}{x})\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =2 \\\\ \\frac{1}{x}(\\frac{1}{y}-1)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =2 \\\\ (\\frac{1}{y}-1)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =2x \\\\ \\int (\\frac{1}{y}-1)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|-y & ={x}^{2}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now apply the initial condition $y(1)=1$ to find $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|1|-1 & ={1}^{2}+C \\\\ 0-1 & =1+C \\\\ C & =-2\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus the particular solution of $(\\frac{1}{xy}-\\frac{1}{x})\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=2$ that satisfies the condition $y(1)=1$ in implicit form is\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|-y={x}^{2}-2\\,.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186240791 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2c2258f7-1c89-5ddf-b3f5-be41b960a73f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{x}{1+x-{x}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238450} {:answer/id #uuid "783d1f44-8f84-5b7c-88aa-9989c97b87f4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{x}{2+2x-{x}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239096} {:answer/id #uuid "96fd893a-6a0d-574c-96a1-9c7c9ecdd73f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{x}{2x+{x}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239359} {:answer/id #uuid "c1af356d-96a3-5dbc-a694-254027046ada" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{x}{{x}^{2}-2x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239753} {:answer/id #uuid "e73db678-16bb-58f9-861b-b9f4c455ff5c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-\\frac{x}{1+x+{x}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240090}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2c2258f7-1c89-5ddf-b3f5-be41b960a73f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{x}{1+x-{x}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238450} :answer-field/id #uuid "288ef88e-ee76-5cb6-ba28-c9169ad97783" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240401}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5f5fc67b-8b37-59a0-97e4-36b78ca0108f" :question/math-academy-id "q-104059" :question/problem "Find the particular solution to the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{x}^{2}}+{y}^{2}$ that satisfies $y(-1)=1.$" :question/worked-solution "We first find the general solution and then apply the given initial condition to find a particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{x}^{2}}+{y}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}+1 \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}+1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}\\text{d}y & =\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x+\\int \\,\\text{d}x \\\\ -\\frac{1}{y} & =-\\frac{1}{x}+x+C \\\\ \\frac{1}{y} & =\\frac{1-{x}^{2}-Cx}{x} \\\\ y & =\\frac{x}{1-{x}^{2}-Cx}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe conclude that the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\frac{x}{1-{x}^{2}-Cx},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an arbitrary constant. \n\nWe now apply the initial condition $y(-1)=1$ to find $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(-1) & =1 \\\\ \\frac{-1}{1-(-1)^{2}-C(-1)} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{-1}{C} & =1 \\\\ C & =-1\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus the particular solution of $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{x}^{2}}+{y}^{2}$ that satisfies the condition $y(-1)=1$ is\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{x}{1+x-{x}^{2}}\\,.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186240793 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "481424ef-2c74-5499-af3e-08e3dea9c7d3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}-{x}^{4}+16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238682} {:answer/id #uuid "53af9c48-3c28-5879-bbf4-c5ba3f2cb694" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{1}{{x}^{4}+{x}^{3}-16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238773} {:answer/id #uuid "5acef49e-76b6-5522-ba50-3922470f8f96" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{1}{2{x}^{3}+2{x}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238841} {:answer/id #uuid "b94a09be-43ba-5aaa-bb0c-be4b94983aec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}-{x}^{2}+4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239666} {:answer/id #uuid "e2fc50d5-241e-5e44-b681-3a645594909e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{1}{{x}^{4}-{x}^{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240052}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e2fc50d5-241e-5e44-b681-3a645594909e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{1}{{x}^{4}-{x}^{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240052} :answer-field/id #uuid "4ffbe1bf-6c6b-54f5-a9b6-580dcd3d52fb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240473}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "04d08db5-75c0-5a9e-a376-151cc06be633" :question/math-academy-id "q-104064" :question/problem "Find the particular solution to the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=3{y}^{2}{x}^{2}-4{y}^{2}{x}^{3}$ that satisfies $y(2)=\\frac{1}{8}.$" :question/worked-solution "We first find the general solution and then apply the given initial condition to find a particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =3{y}^{2}{x}^{2}-4{y}^{2}{x}^{3} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={y}^{2}(3{x}^{2}-4{x}^{3}) \\\\ \\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =3{x}^{2}-4{x}^{3} \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (3{x}^{2}-4{x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y & =3\\int {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x-4\\int {x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ -\\frac{1}{y} & ={x}^{3}-{x}^{4}+C \\\\ y & =\\frac{1}{{x}^{4}-{x}^{3}-C}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now apply the initial condition $y(2)=\\frac{1}{8}$ to find $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(2) & =\\frac{1}{8} \\\\ \\frac{1}{{2}^{4}-{2}^{3}-C} & =\\frac{1}{8} \\\\ \\frac{1}{8-C} & =\\frac{1}{8} \\\\ C & =0\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus the particular solution of $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=3{y}^{2}{x}^{2}-4{y}^{2}{x}^{3}$ that satisfies the condition $y(2)=\\frac{1}{8}$ is\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{1}{{x}^{4}-{x}^{3}}\\,.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186240794 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "75be7c90-32ab-5c64-906d-1dd7954d2121" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)+4{x}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239071} {:answer/id #uuid "82693f98-0710-5635-895b-2a14d84f4e9d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+4{x}^{2}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239189} {:answer/id #uuid "cd7da46f-6bf6-5179-ad99-a6c9aa84ab9a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+8{x}^{2}-{\\pi }^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239852} {:answer/id #uuid "f3ba6483-6e8b-5e55-93bc-ce43b1b86246" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)+8{x}^{2}-{\\pi }^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240204} {:answer/id #uuid "f3c87060-4f09-5b9a-ba36-024d4f3b3691" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+4{x}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240205}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "75be7c90-32ab-5c64-906d-1dd7954d2121" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)+4{x}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239071} :answer-field/id #uuid "7c9d1e6a-7b24-50e3-9ef5-4dad3d944987" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240555}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "cdddaa9b-4174-550d-a7b6-1b8e1a3f2b29" :question/math-academy-id "q-104065" :question/problem "Find the particular solution to the differential equation $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-8x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ that satisfies $y(\\frac{\\pi }{2})={\\pi }^{2}.$ Assume that $0<x<\\pi .$" :question/worked-solution "We first find the general solution and then apply the given initial condition to find a particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-8x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡x \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+8x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}+8x \\\\ \\int \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}+8x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\,\\text{d}y & =\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x+8\\int x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x+4{x}^{2}+{C}_{1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo calculate the integral on the right-hand side of this equality, we use a substitution\n\n$$\nu=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nThen  we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x) \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u|+{C}_{2} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)+{C}_{2},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere we used that $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x>0.$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\ny=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)+4{x}^{2}+C.\n$$\n\nwhere $C={C}_{1}+{C}_{2}$ is an arbitrary constant. \n\nWe now apply the initial condition $y(\\frac{\\pi }{2})={\\pi }^{2}$ to find $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(\\frac{\\pi }{2}) & ={\\pi }^{2} \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\frac{\\pi }{2})+4{(\\frac{\\pi }{2})}^{2}+C & ={\\pi }^{2} \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡1+{\\pi }^{2}+C & ={\\pi }^{2} \\\\ C & =0\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus the particular solution of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-8x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ that satisfies the condition $y(\\frac{\\pi }{2})={\\pi }^{2}$ is\n\n$$\ny=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)+4{x}^{2}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272362 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0a4171c5-a734-541a-8466-69b56ce0d873" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1+{e}^{x})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269359} {:answer/id #uuid "38ecd45c-ba43-5032-b302-2a4db3f68db3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1+x+{e}^{x})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269785} {:answer/id #uuid "b0aa3d76-7de4-57d1-9a49-fedf8212ceab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+{e}^{x})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270846} {:answer/id #uuid "b2780b36-6d65-5d14-9b03-a066bbecba37" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3-2x-{e}^{x})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270864} {:answer/id #uuid "bcf951d6-95fc-5d3d-8bf4-6811a7297a18" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3-{e}^{x})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270934}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bcf951d6-95fc-5d3d-8bf4-6811a7297a18" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3-{e}^{x})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270934} :answer-field/id #uuid "c146e3ac-1df2-5b81-bf01-9382213bcac9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271861}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4a8c132a-a85d-5f19-bf08-0d6e90b34efd" :question/math-academy-id "q-14267" :question/problem "Find the specific solution to the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={e}^{x+y}$ given that  $\\,y(0)=-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2.$" :question/worked-solution "We first find the general solution and then apply the given initial condition to find a particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={e}^{x+y} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={e}^{x}{e}^{y} \\\\ {e}^{-y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={e}^{x} \\\\ \\int {e}^{-y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int {e}^{-y}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int {e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ -{e}^{-y} & ={e}^{x}+{C}_{1} \\\\ {e}^{-y} & =-{e}^{x}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the natural logarithm to both sides, we find the general solution:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{-y}) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(-{e}^{x}+C) \\\\ -y & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(C-{e}^{x}) \\\\ y & =-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(C-{e}^{x}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now apply the condition $y(0)=-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2$ to find $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(0) & =-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2 \\\\ -\\operatorname{ln}⁡(C-{e}^{0}) & =-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2 \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡(C-1) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡2 \\\\ C-1 & =2 \\\\ C & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus the particular solution of $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={e}^{x+y}$ that satisfies the condition $y(0)=-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2$ is\n\n$$\ny=-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3-{e}^{x}).\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186320759 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4fe73586-88cc-5eb9-b551-265a21f8d21c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}(2{x}^{3}-x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319625}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4fe73586-88cc-5eb9-b551-265a21f8d21c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}(2{x}^{3}-x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319625} :answer-field/id #uuid "138ff64c-aba6-5818-815e-c8ab6507d894" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320202}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1e6d2e79-6130-55ee-82e5-9a200a11282e" :question/math-academy-id "q-350957" :question/problem "Find the particular solution to the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{e}^{-y}=6{x}^{2}{e}^{-y}$ that satisfies $y(1)=0.$\n\n$y(x)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We first find the general solution and then apply the given initial condition to find a particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{e}^{-y} & =6{x}^{2}{e}^{-y} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =6{x}^{2}{e}^{-y}-{e}^{-y} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =(6{x}^{2}-1){e}^{-y} \\\\ {e}^{y}\\,\\text{d}y & =(6{x}^{2}-1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int {e}^{y}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int (6{x}^{2}-1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ {e}^{y} & =2{x}^{3}-x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the natural logarithm to both sides, we find the general solution:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{y}) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2{x}^{3}-x+C) \\\\ y & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2{x}^{3}-x+C)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now apply the initial condition $y(1)=0$ to find $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(1) & =0 \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡(2\\cdot {1}^{3}-1+C) & =0 \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡(1+C) & =0 \\\\ C & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the particular solution is\n\n$$\ny(x)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2{x}^{3}-x).\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186323687 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f64a635e-2029-5d66-8938-817f402fbc99" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{x}+4{x}^{2}+7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323077}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f64a635e-2029-5d66-8938-817f402fbc99" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{x}+4{x}^{2}+7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323077} :answer-field/id #uuid "3d3128ea-a07c-5f2f-ad3f-00a6446136d1" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323290}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6e98fc5d-ad7f-574e-b282-efe5e38c1e1b" :question/math-academy-id "q-355546" :question/problem "Find the particular solution to the differential equation ${x}^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-8{x}^{3}=5$ that satisfies $y(1)=6.$\n\n$y(x)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We first find the general solution and then apply the given initial condition to find a particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-8{x}^{3} & =5 \\\\ {x}^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =5+8{x}^{3} \\\\ \\text{d}y & =(5{x}^{-2}+8x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\text{d}y & =\\int (5{x}^{-2}+8x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =-5{x}^{-1}+4{x}^{2}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now apply the initial condition $y(1)=6$ to find $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(1) & =6 \\\\ -5(1)^{-1}+4(1)^{2}+C & =6 \\\\ C-1 & =6 \\\\ C & =7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the particular solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(x) & =-5{x}^{-1}+4{x}^{2}+7 \\\\  & =-\\frac{5}{x}+4{x}^{2}+7.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186323688 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "13eaf0de-4e0e-5ea8-907d-4d9968125b18" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6\\sqrt{x}+2{x}^{2}+3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321308}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "13eaf0de-4e0e-5ea8-907d-4d9968125b18" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6\\sqrt{x}+2{x}^{2}+3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321308} :answer-field/id #uuid "dc4ee59c-22f5-5a40-b03d-278d405cc912" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323609}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "75023361-eb11-537e-8a6b-dbd0dee1ad40" :question/math-academy-id "q-355547" :question/problem "Find the particular solution to the differential equation $\\sqrt{x}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-4x\\sqrt{x}=3$ that satisfies $y(1)=11.$\n\n$y(x)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We first find the general solution and then apply the given initial condition to find a particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{x}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-4x\\sqrt{x} & =3 \\\\ \\sqrt{x}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =3+4x\\sqrt{x} \\\\ \\text{d}y & =(3{x}^{-1/2}+4x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\text{d}y & =\\int (3{x}^{-1/2}+4x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =6{x}^{1/2}+2{x}^{2}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now apply the initial condition $y(1)=11$ to find $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(1) & =11 \\\\ 6(1)^{1/2}+2(1)^{2}+C & =11 \\\\ C+8 & =11 \\\\ C & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the particular solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(x) & =6{x}^{1/2}+2{x}^{2}+3 \\\\  & =6\\sqrt{x}+2{x}^{2}+3.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186323689 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2055e3dd-2e6d-5b82-b38d-ca3921647471" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2{e}^{2{x}^{2}}-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321390}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2055e3dd-2e6d-5b82-b38d-ca3921647471" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2{e}^{2{x}^{2}}-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321390} :answer-field/id #uuid "0f37f1d2-7d30-5928-8c23-707d4ffb2cc7" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323197}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "af7393d2-efb0-5146-b448-33e99ed4412d" :question/math-academy-id "q-355559" :question/problem "Find the particular solution to the differential equation $2y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-4x{y}^{2}=4x$ that satisfies $y(0)=1.$ Assume that $y>0.$\n\n$y(x)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We first find the general solution and then apply the given initial condition to find a particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-4x{y}^{2} & =4x \\\\ 2y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =4x{y}^{2}+4x \\\\ 2y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =4x({y}^{2}+1) \\\\ \\frac{2y}{{y}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}y & =4x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{2y}{{y}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int 4x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡({y}^{2}+1) & =2{x}^{2}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExponentiating both sides, we find the general solution:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡({y}^{2}+1)} & ={e}^{2{x}^{2}+C} \\\\ {y}^{2}+1 & =C{e}^{2{x}^{2}} \\\\ y & =\\sqrt{C{e}^{2{x}^{2}}-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere we used that $y>0.$\n\nWe now apply the initial condition $y(0)=1$ to find $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(0) & =1 \\\\ \\sqrt{C{e}^{2(0)^{2}}-1} & =1 \\\\ \\sqrt{C-1} & =1 \\\\ C-1 & =1 \\\\ C & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the particular solution is\n\n$$\ny(x)=\\sqrt{2{e}^{2{x}^{2}}-1}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186323691 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "11d2d065-70d1-5174-a4e1-728f26ee993f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2x-1){e}^{2x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321286}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "11d2d065-70d1-5174-a4e1-728f26ee993f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2x-1){e}^{2x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321286} :answer-field/id #uuid "a70e7a74-f88a-5b4f-8fac-b4f7d571a35d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323490}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "aabfb888-4d5b-5ee3-a31d-caf8a930a357" :question/math-academy-id "q-355564" :question/problem "Find the particular solution to the differential equation $(-\\frac{1}{xy}+\\frac{2}{y})\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=4$ that satisfies $y(1)={e}^{2}.$\n\n$y(x)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We first find the general solution and then apply the given initial condition to find a particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-\\frac{1}{xy}+\\frac{2}{y})\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =4 \\\\ \\frac{2x-1}{xy}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =4 \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{4x}{2x-1} \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =2+\\frac{2}{2x-1} \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\text{d}y & =(2+\\frac{2}{2x-1})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int (2+\\frac{2}{2x-1})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|y| & =2x+\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2x-1|+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the exponential function to both sides, we find the general solution:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|} & ={e}^{2x+\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2x-1|+C} \\\\ |y| & ={e}^{2x+\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2x-1|+C} \\\\ |y| & ={e}^{2x}\\cdot {e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2x-1|}\\cdot {e}^{C} \\\\ y & =K(2x-1){e}^{2x},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K=\\pm {e}^{C}$ is an arbitrary constant. \n\nWe now apply the initial condition $y(1)={e}^{2}$ to find $K:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(1) & ={e}^{2} \\\\ K(2(1)-1){e}^{2(1)} & ={e}^{2} \\\\ K{e}^{2} & ={e}^{2} \\\\ K & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the particular solution is\n\n$$\ny(x)=(2x-1){e}^{2x}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186323692 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "90c5bd0e-992a-5060-a1b1-7adb29cef3ca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{-{e}^{-2x}+2{e}^{2}+1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322298}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "90c5bd0e-992a-5060-a1b1-7adb29cef3ca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{-{e}^{-2x}+2{e}^{2}+1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322298} :answer-field/id #uuid "15f6b0da-0d33-5c51-ac9b-a4198b00fb73" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323209}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "805542c0-bca8-5f60-bf27-701c39eb6996" :question/math-academy-id "q-355576" :question/problem "Find the specific solution to the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={e}^{-2x-y}$ given that  $\\,y(0)=2.$\n\n$y(x)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡($\n{{field-1}} $)$" :question/worked-solution "We first find the general solution and then apply the given initial condition to find a particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={e}^{-2x-y} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={e}^{-2x}{e}^{-y} \\\\ {e}^{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={e}^{-2x} \\\\ \\int {e}^{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {e}^{-2x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int {e}^{y}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int {e}^{-2x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ {e}^{y} & =-\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{-2x}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the natural logarithm to both sides, we find the general solution:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{y}) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(-\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{-2x}+C) \\\\ y & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(-\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{-2x}+C).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now apply the condition $y(0)=2$ to find $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(0) & =2 \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡(-\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{0}+C) & =2 \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡(C-\\frac{1}{2}) & =2 \\\\ C-\\frac{1}{2} & ={e}^{2} \\\\ C & =\\frac{2{e}^{2}+1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus the particular solution of $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={e}^{-2x-y}$ that satisfies the condition $y(0)=2$ is\n\n$$\ny=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{-{e}^{-2x}+2{e}^{2}+1}{2}).\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186323693 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7cecbd4b-7276-5711-93be-756561f37cee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}(\\frac{5}{4}-{e}^{-x})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322129}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7cecbd4b-7276-5711-93be-756561f37cee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}(\\frac{5}{4}-{e}^{-x})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322129} :answer-field/id #uuid "19779a17-730f-59fa-bfa1-c2bc8e54d880" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323218}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a6ea94de-6671-5cd2-9382-54cb9545def9" :question/math-academy-id "q-355577" :question/problem "Find the specific solution to the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={e}^{-x-y}$ given that $\\,y(0)=-\\operatorname{ln}⁡4.$\n\n$y(x)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We first find the general solution and then apply the given initial condition to find a particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={e}^{-x-y} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={e}^{-x}{e}^{-y} \\\\ {e}^{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={e}^{-x} \\\\ \\int {e}^{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {e}^{-x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int {e}^{y}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int {e}^{-x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ {e}^{y} & =-{e}^{-x}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the natural logarithm to both sides, we find the general solution:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{y}) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(-{e}^{-x}+C) \\\\ y & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(-{e}^{-x}+C).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now apply the condition $y(0)=-\\operatorname{ln}⁡4$ to find $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(0) & =-\\operatorname{ln}⁡4 \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡(-{e}^{0}+C) & =-\\operatorname{ln}⁡4 \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡(C-1) & =-\\operatorname{ln}⁡4 \\\\ C-1 & =\\frac{1}{4} \\\\ C & =\\frac{5}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus the particular solution of $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={e}^{-x-y}$ that satisfies the condition $y(0)=-\\operatorname{ln}⁡4$ is\n\n$$\ny=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{5}{4}-{e}^{-x}).\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186323696 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2d94f85d-4906-5228-9ed0-d96a48b11c86" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}(2-{e}^{-x})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321501}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2d94f85d-4906-5228-9ed0-d96a48b11c86" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}(2-{e}^{-x})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321501} :answer-field/id #uuid "6e8e425b-6779-5e93-9532-18cad7118f4f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323392}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b704df68-ffc0-57d3-acee-bb78600fdc0b" :question/math-academy-id "q-355582" :question/problem "Find the specific solution to the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={e}^{-x-y}$ given that  $\\,y(0)=0.$\n\n$y(x)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We first find the general solution and then apply the given initial condition to find a particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={e}^{-x-y} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={e}^{-x}{e}^{-y} \\\\ {e}^{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={e}^{-x} \\\\ \\int {e}^{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {e}^{-x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int {e}^{y}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int {e}^{-x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ {e}^{y} & =-{e}^{-x}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the natural logarithm to both sides, we find the general solution:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{y}) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(-{e}^{-x}+C) \\\\ y & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(-{e}^{-x}+C).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now apply the condition $y(0)=0$ to find $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(0) & =0 \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡(-{e}^{0}+C) & =0 \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡(C-1) & =0 \\\\ C-1 & =1 \\\\ C & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus the particular solution of $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={e}^{-x-y}$ that satisfies the condition $y(0)=0$ is\n\n$$\ny=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2-{e}^{-x}).\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186326809 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "502004df-a0be-5cea-878e-09803c5e34d8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2{e}^{x}-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324628} {:answer/id #uuid "5babf9ef-2007-5ac3-b1a7-d3a7000142a9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2-{e}^{x})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324728} {:answer/id #uuid "9f32f367-c166-57dd-a1ca-a5e258aafc79" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325321} {:answer/id #uuid "cb26728e-8a5c-5d88-940f-50ca2ae95d4f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{{e}^{x}+1}{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325734} {:answer/id #uuid "f04334c1-fe98-564e-8bda-076b98d63f11" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4{e}^{x}-3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326091}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "502004df-a0be-5cea-878e-09803c5e34d8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2{e}^{x}-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324628} :answer-field/id #uuid "2fa3b410-49d2-532c-b067-882d1961f404" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326303}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "45459917-ee60-5543-8543-ded7c1f55344" :question/math-academy-id "q-4016" :question/problem "Find the particular solution to the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={e}^{x-2y}$ that satisfies $y(0)=0.$" :question/worked-solution "We first find the general solution and then apply the given initial condition to find a particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={e}^{x-2y} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={e}^{x}\\cdot {e}^{-2y} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{{e}^{x}}{{e}^{2y}} \\\\ {e}^{2y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={e}^{x} \\\\ \\int {e}^{2y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int {e}^{2y}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int {e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}{e}^{2y} & ={e}^{x}+{C}_{1} \\\\ {e}^{2y} & =2{e}^{x}+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C=2{C}_{1}$ is an arbitrary constant.\n\nApplying the natural logarithm to both sides, we find the general solution:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{2y}) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2{e}^{x}+C) \\\\ y & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2{e}^{x}+C).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now apply the condition $y(0)=0$ to find $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(0) & =0 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2{e}^{0}+C) & =0 \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡(2+C) & =0 \\\\ 2+C & =1 \\\\ C & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus the particular solution of $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={e}^{x-2y}$ that satisfies the condition $y(0)=0$ is\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2{e}^{x}-1).\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348217 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2c251d4a-f0c0-5a48-8e3e-7592f3c7a8d0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=x+{e}^{-3x}-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345744} {:answer/id #uuid "5e801574-e220-5db2-a084-a19a5433b090" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={x}^{2}-3{e}^{-x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346166} {:answer/id #uuid "781de7e7-abc0-5010-a18b-6acb28d569ae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={x}^{2}-3{e}^{-x}+2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346405} {:answer/id #uuid "d8d86e1b-6bec-5f73-8e1e-04c4c97f4533" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=4x+{e}^{-3x}-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347262} {:answer/id #uuid "ec8bcfe8-08ab-5bf7-879a-4e9b26f6d9cd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-2{e}^{-x}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347438}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5e801574-e220-5db2-a084-a19a5433b090" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={x}^{2}-3{e}^{-x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346166} :answer-field/id #uuid "a5f056d2-0c8e-5224-b4ba-23c1cec61974" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347897}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d0357fe4-4d50-5037-a26c-ebfd87a1a2f3" :question/math-academy-id "q-79371" :question/problem "Find the particular solution to the differential equation ${e}^{x}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-2x{e}^{x}=3$ that satisfies $y(0)=-3.$" :question/worked-solution "We first find the general solution and then apply the given initial condition to find a particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{x}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-2x{e}^{x} & =3 \\\\ {e}^{x}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =3+2x{e}^{x} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =3{e}^{-x}+2x \\\\ \\int \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (3{e}^{-x}+2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\,\\text{d}y & =\\int 3{e}^{-x}\\,\\text{d}x+\\int 2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =-3{e}^{-x}+{x}^{2}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now apply the initial condition $y(0)=-3$ to find $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(0) & =-3 \\\\ -3{e}^{-0}+{0}^{2}+C & =-3 \\\\ C-3 & =-3 \\\\ C & =0\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus the particular solution of ${e}^{x}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-2x{e}^{x}=3$ that satisfies the condition $y(0)=-3$ is\n\n$$\ny={x}^{2}-3{e}^{-x}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348218 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "451f3842-16b6-5866-9651-73784c8644e3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{{x}^{4}-x+2}{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345950} {:answer/id #uuid "58be30d8-ef50-5ef7-b5f3-523380bbc11f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{{x}^{2}+1}{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346113} {:answer/id #uuid "70a616da-72b0-575c-adfa-c326848aeb16" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+2x-2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346340} {:answer/id #uuid "816eafe7-746e-5226-88e6-c6e7b7b43820" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{4}-x+1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346482} {:answer/id #uuid "f1baeeb1-4f87-5895-9e67-a1a7e8844e32" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{4}-x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347490}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "816eafe7-746e-5226-88e6-c6e7b7b43820" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{4}-x+1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346482} :answer-field/id #uuid "ea329cec-2c85-5a3c-ae6a-b47fc15cd1cd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348015}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "49fb438b-3c89-5f2d-ad22-0703828a1cf7" :question/math-academy-id "q-79373" :question/problem "Find the particular solution to the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{e}^{-y}=4{x}^{3}{e}^{-y}$ that satisfies $y(1)=0.$" :question/worked-solution "We first find the general solution and then apply the given initial condition to find a particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{e}^{-y} & =4{x}^{3}{e}^{-y} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =4{x}^{3}{e}^{-y}-{e}^{-y} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =(4{x}^{3}-1){e}^{-y} \\\\ {e}^{y}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =4{x}^{3}-1 \\\\ \\int {e}^{y}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (4{x}^{3}-1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int {e}^{y}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int (4{x}^{3}-1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ {e}^{y} & ={x}^{4}-x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the natural logarithm to both sides, we find the general solution:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{y}) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{4}-x+C) \\\\ y & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{4}-x+C)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now apply the initial condition $y(1)=0$ to find $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(1) & =0 \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡({1}^{4}-1+C) & =0 \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡C & =0 \\\\ C & =1\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus the particular solution of $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{e}^{-y}=4{x}^{3}{e}^{-y}$ that satisfies the condition $y(1)=0$ is\n\n$$\ny=\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{4}-x+1).\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348224 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "02894820-667a-5bb1-8d2d-4a0e95595d4e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y}^{2}=3{e}^{x}-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345370} {:answer/id #uuid "1d756a9d-9a70-50be-87ba-3a12ce907a55" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y}^{2}=2{e}^{{x}^{2}}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345607} {:answer/id #uuid "4914777d-f2b5-57b0-a44a-c23834802afd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=2{e}^{x}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345974} {:answer/id #uuid "b5d0bd7d-ae6a-5b73-af44-998074dd148c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y}^{3}={e}^{{x}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346935} {:answer/id #uuid "d13ddd57-da35-5009-922f-44e87553a2f0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y}^{3}=3{e}^{{x}^{2}}-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347184}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d13ddd57-da35-5009-922f-44e87553a2f0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y}^{3}=3{e}^{{x}^{2}}-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347184} :answer-field/id #uuid "d0ce2963-49b7-5510-bb64-1ea4168634e2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347969}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "64550cf0-ae14-5b89-b54c-860d29b3d527" :question/math-academy-id "q-79425" :question/problem "Find the particular solution to the differential equation $3{y}^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-2x{y}^{3}=4x$ that satisfies $y(0)=1.$  Assume that $y>0.$" :question/worked-solution "We first find the general solution and then apply the given initial condition to find a particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{y}^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-2x{y}^{3} & =4x \\\\ 3{y}^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =2x(2+{y}^{3}) \\\\ \\frac{3{y}^{2}}{2+{y}^{3}}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =2x \\\\ \\int \\frac{3{y}^{2}}{2+{y}^{3}}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{3{y}^{2}}{2+{y}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}y & ={x}^{2}+{C}_{1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo calculate the integral on the left-hand side of this equality, we use a substitution\n\n$$\nu=2+{y}^{3}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}u=3{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y.\n$$\n\nThen  we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{3{y}^{2}}{2+{y}^{3}}\\text{d}y & =\\int \\frac{1}{2+{y}^{3}}(3{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y) \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u|+{C}_{2} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2+{y}^{3})+{C}_{2},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere we used that $y>0.$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2+{y}^{3})+{C}_{2} & ={x}^{2}+{C}_{1} \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡(2+{y}^{3}) & ={x}^{2}+{C}_{1}-{C}_{2} \\\\ {e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2+{y}^{3})} & ={e}^{{x}^{2}+{C}_{1}-{C}_{2}} \\\\ 2+{y}^{3} & =K{e}^{{x}^{2}} \\\\ {y}^{3} & =K{e}^{{x}^{2}}-2,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K=\\pm {e}^{{C}_{1}-{C}_{2}}$ is an arbitrary constant. \n\nWe now apply the initial condition $y(0)=1$ to find $K:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{1}^{3} & =K{e}^{{0}^{2}}-2 \\\\ 1 & =K-2 \\\\ K & =3\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we get the particular solution in implicit form:\n\n$$\n{y}^{3}=3{e}^{{x}^{2}}-2.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186373003 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cad08fd0-a60c-5289-bfae-917d24b4cf51" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4-x-{x}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373005}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cad08fd0-a60c-5289-bfae-917d24b4cf51" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4-x-{x}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373005} :answer-field/id #uuid "c01b75b0-e7f0-5237-8118-7d26642ee499" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373004}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c1491d28-f486-5d5a-8bd7-310f4893ab88" :question/math-academy-id "q-355560" :question/problem "Find the particular solution to the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{4{y}^{2}}{{x}^{2}}+{y}^{2}$ that satisfies $y(2)=-1.$\n\n|  | $y(x)=$ | $x$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | {{field-1}} |" :question/worked-solution "We first find the general solution and then apply the given initial condition to find a particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{4{y}^{2}}{{x}^{2}}+{y}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={y}^{2}(\\frac{4}{{x}^{2}}+1) \\\\ \\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y & =(4{x}^{-2}+1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int {y}^{-2}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int (4{x}^{-2}+1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ -{y}^{-1} & =-4{x}^{-1}+x+C \\\\ -\\frac{1}{y} & =-\\frac{4}{x}+x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving for $y$, we find the general solution:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{y} & =\\frac{4}{x}-x-C \\\\ \\frac{1}{y} & =\\frac{4-{x}^{2}-Cx}{x} \\\\ y & =\\frac{x}{4-{x}^{2}-Cx}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now apply the initial condition $y(2)=-1$ to find $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(2) & =-1 \\\\ \\frac{2}{4-{2}^{2}-C(2)} & =-1 \\\\ \\frac{2}{-2C} & =-1 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{C} & =-1 \\\\ C & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the particular solution is\n\n$$\ny(x)=\\frac{x}{4-x-{x}^{2}}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186373526 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e0ba7021-278a-5bfc-8d11-f00a3b63b0b4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-{e}^{-x}-4x+8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373528} {:answer/id #uuid "0d863f80-974c-5fd0-9ba0-3d19bf8e3347" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={e}^{-x}-2{x}^{2}+6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373529} {:answer/id #uuid "22f9d7b5-6e34-51ba-a04a-13901fa9651e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={e}^{x}-4{x}^{2}+6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373530} {:answer/id #uuid "31b7712a-30c7-5b25-a8c1-60f541081385" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={e}^{x}-2{x}^{2}+6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373531} {:answer/id #uuid "fc9220a2-0ad7-50c6-85ed-98e053e99e0b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-{e}^{-x}-2{x}^{2}+8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373532}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fc9220a2-0ad7-50c6-85ed-98e053e99e0b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-{e}^{-x}-2{x}^{2}+8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373532} :answer-field/id #uuid "be7c8072-e10a-55ab-8358-3a565f0a6a95" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373527}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8fdc31d5-5a66-5e44-b1bd-e6668f2e6e14" :question/math-academy-id "q-104056" :question/problem "Find the particular solution to the differential equation ${e}^{x}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+4x{e}^{x}=1$ that satisfies $y(0)=7.$" :question/worked-solution "We first find the general solution and then apply the given initial condition to find a particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{x}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+4x{e}^{x} & =1 \\\\ {e}^{x}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =1-4x{e}^{x} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={e}^{-x}-4x \\\\ \\int \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int ({e}^{-x}-4x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\,\\text{d}y & =\\int {e}^{-x}\\,\\text{d}x-4\\int x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =-{e}^{-x}-2{x}^{2}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now apply the initial condition $y(0)=7$ to find $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(0) & =7 \\\\ -{e}^{-0}+2\\cdot {0}^{2}+C & =7 \\\\ C-1 & =7 \\\\ C & =8\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus the particular solution of ${e}^{x}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+4x{e}^{x}=1$ that satisfies the condition $y(0)=7$ is\n\n$$\ny=-{e}^{-x}-2{x}^{2}+8.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186373533 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0ddf8e77-1f92-52ca-ba0f-d3a0c8aeeddd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3}-{x}^{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373535} {:answer/id #uuid "ddeef60e-4ec8-586c-a724-ac4e52f99051" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3}-{x}^{2}+e)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373536} {:answer/id #uuid "eaeab17a-7de9-520a-be72-1e945c3a28b3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{{x}^{3}-{x}^{2}+2e}{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373537} {:answer/id #uuid "a08229ef-ec6b-54f8-8faf-e2cb18e885e7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+2x-3+e)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373538} {:answer/id #uuid "9474dc52-92f4-5600-a6ca-5868d826ebe0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{e{x}^{2}+e}{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373539}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ddeef60e-4ec8-586c-a724-ac4e52f99051" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3}-{x}^{2}+e)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373536} :answer-field/id #uuid "493ad9d4-8aff-5cd3-bb25-1648834bbb25" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373534}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "52066178-466b-57ba-8963-0e5e66a7bec7" :question/math-academy-id "q-104057" :question/problem "Find the particular solution to the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+2x{e}^{-y}=3{x}^{2}{e}^{-y}$ that satisfies $y(1)=1.$" :question/worked-solution "We first find the general solution and then apply the given initial condition to find a particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+2x{e}^{-y} & =3{x}^{2}{e}^{-y} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =3{x}^{2}{e}^{-y}-2x{e}^{-y} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =(3{x}^{2}-2x){e}^{-y} \\\\ {e}^{y}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =3{x}^{2}-2x \\\\ \\int {e}^{y}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (3{x}^{2}-2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int {e}^{y}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int (3{x}^{2}-2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ {e}^{y} & ={x}^{3}-{x}^{2}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the natural logarithm to both sides, we find the general solution:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{y}) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3}-{x}^{2}+C) \\\\ y & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3}-{x}^{2}+C)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now apply the initial condition $y(1)=1$ to find $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(1) & =1 \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡({1}^{3}-{1}^{2}+C) & =1 \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡C & =1 \\\\ C & =e\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus the particular solution of $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+2x{e}^{-y}=3{x}^{2}{e}^{-y}$ that satisfies the condition $y(1)=1$ is\n\n$$\ny=\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3}-{x}^{2}+e).\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186404231 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "aa22294c-97df-59d3-a2ef-bb723379bd93" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={e}^{3{x}^{3}+{x}^{2}-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186404233} {:answer/id #uuid "05c76659-9ee2-5ea1-9921-4c61064bc47c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={e}^{({x}^{3}+{x}^{2}-2)/3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186404234} {:answer/id #uuid "d957c339-7d86-5b49-bfb4-f34772448576" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={e}^{(2{x}^{3}+{x}^{2}-1)/3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186404235} {:answer/id #uuid "59acccda-8ad0-5671-8d3b-1eba77285637" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={e}^{{x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}-5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186404236} {:answer/id #uuid "08886f8e-1110-502c-b6b0-62359e9dd0d0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={e}^{({x}^{3}+3{x}^{2}-4)/3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186404237}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "08886f8e-1110-502c-b6b0-62359e9dd0d0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={e}^{({x}^{3}+3{x}^{2}-4)/3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186404237} :answer-field/id #uuid "5399864b-fdb6-560a-bb1c-eadfa2e8485b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186404232}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "177e97c5-b0fe-5fdf-abe1-80b42d3faf53" :question/math-academy-id "q-8306" :question/problem "Find the particular solution to the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=2yx+y{x}^{2}$ that satisfies $y(1)=1.$" :question/worked-solution "We first find the general solution and then apply the given initial condition to find a particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =2yx+y{x}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =y(2x+{x}^{2}) \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =2x+{x}^{2} \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (2x+{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\text{d}y & =2\\int x\\,\\text{d}x+\\int {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|y| & ={x}^{2}+\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the natural logarithm to both sides, we find the general solution:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|} & ={e}^{{x}^{2}+{x}^{3}/3+C} \\\\ |y| & ={e}^{{x}^{2}+{x}^{3}/3+C} \\\\ y & =\\pm {e}^{{x}^{2}+{x}^{3}/3+C} \\\\ y & =K{e}^{{x}^{2}+{x}^{3}/3},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K=\\pm {e}^{C}$ is an arbitrary constant. \n\nWe now apply the initial condition $y(1)=1$ to find $K:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(1) & =1 \\\\ K{e}^{{1}^{2}+{1}^{3}/3} & =1 \\\\ K{e}^{4/3} & =1 \\\\ K & ={e}^{-4/3}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus the particular solution of $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=2yx+y{x}^{2}$ that satisfies the condition $y(1)=1$ is\n\n$$\ny={e}^{-4/3}\\cdot {e}^{{x}^{2}+{x}^{3}/3}={e}^{({x}^{3}+3{x}^{2}-4)/3}\\,.\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Finding Particular Solutions of Differential Equations by First Rearranging and Then Separating"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100951 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100795 :question/id #uuid "f5ffa549-e77e-5db4-9fde-5b0134957539" :question/math-academy-id "e-8732" :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x} = \\dfrac{3y}{x}, \\qquad y(-1) = -2.\n$$\n\nYou're given that $y = Ax^3$ is the solution to this initial value problem. What is the value of the constant $A?$" :question/worked-solution "We're given that $y = Ax^3$ is the solution to the initial value problem. Therefore, it must satisfy the differential equation *and* the initial condition $y(-1) = -2.$\n\nSubstituting the initial condition $y({\\color{red}{-1}}) = {\\color{blue}{-2}}$ into our solution and solving for $A,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =A{x}^{3} \\\\ -2 & =A(-1)^{3} \\\\ -2 & =A(-1) \\\\ A & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny = 2x^3 .\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "82a9b23c-4c79-56cd-9761-79d0ee22646d" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101156 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d5b5d65b-ec6c-51b7-9cdd-88d75d5264d5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3e" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186098272} {:answer/id #uuid "120fac45-9287-5ac3-9100-a665688ad407" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{e^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186098273} {:answer/id #uuid "2b917d15-1467-52ba-b80f-ce6601b19575" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186098274} {:answer/id #uuid "2fc1975e-b88f-59af-b700-be8515c0465a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3e^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186098275} {:answer/id #uuid "43c462fc-7958-5b11-abe9-5c053ed82ed9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186098276}] :answer-field/id #uuid "e3f720a1-e094-53ee-b045-f9df2b9d62de" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186098271}] :question/id #uuid "42bb61a9-d18d-5d5b-88a0-be6dbf1c9579" :question/math-academy-id "q-141055" :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem\n$\\frac{dy}{dx} = 2y, y(1) = 3$.\n\nYou're given that $y = Ae^{2x}$ is the solution to this initial value problem. What is the value of the constant $A$?"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101159 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8968d782-5c74-5e7b-b779-8cbfc2e7b716" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186098290} {:answer/id #uuid "8cdf33b5-c72f-51a0-b0ca-dbf427183cc7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186098291} {:answer/id #uuid "94b06eab-3c8d-5854-9e4c-da8f5d45c63a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186098292} {:answer/id #uuid "984c5e03-478d-5b00-b114-3fbe4f6f1cce" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186098293} {:answer/id #uuid "4c69d0cf-6289-5358-a8d6-b7b5d72161aa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186098294}] :answer-field/id #uuid "386faf29-f883-5197-a57f-f605f304e704" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186098289}] :question/id #uuid "50fb0b0b-198a-530e-b586-9313a3c7912c" :question/math-academy-id "q-141117" :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem\n$\\frac{dy}{dx} = y^{2}, y(1) = 4$.\n\nYou're given that $y = \\frac{1}{A - x}$ is the solution to this initial value problem. What is the value of the constant $A$?"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272211 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "058d33c3-38bc-5a8a-b193-b57183edaeaf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269316} {:answer/id #uuid "20ca9768-8408-5d47-83d3-3cdeac15ea6a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269546} {:answer/id #uuid "3e9b3f54-9ab3-5a07-8550-6d3a6dd62a49" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269842} {:answer/id #uuid "4db64a33-bfca-52ca-81d7-4627db1c20b9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269972} {:answer/id #uuid "ddb92157-9cb4-5dee-a5ff-fc87722216d2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271216}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ddb92157-9cb4-5dee-a5ff-fc87722216d2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271216} :answer-field/id #uuid "8d9cca69-c36e-5a39-a987-76b027db5270" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271760}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0e6c8b47-d479-53b1-8c84-47f5f3c59cd6" :question/math-academy-id "q-141107" :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{4y}{x},\\,y(-1)=-1.\n$$\n\nYou're given that $y=A{x}^{4}$ is the solution to this initial value problem. What is the value of the constant $A?$" :question/worked-solution "We're given that $y=A{x}^{4}$ is the solution to the initial value problem. Therefore, it must satisfy the differential equation *and* the initial condition $y(-1)=-1.$\n\nSubstituting the initial condition $y(-1)=-1$ into our solution and solving for $A,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =A{x}^{4} \\\\ -1 & =A(-1)^{4} \\\\ -1 & =A(1) \\\\ A & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny=(-1){x}^{4}=-{x}^{4}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272212 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "40d86cd0-b610-5949-970a-9cadba494d80" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269856} {:answer/id #uuid "59db9bef-eba4-5426-bced-b24333ab4c7c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270070} {:answer/id #uuid "9aee7aa9-6233-54c2-97d7-0f70259781ae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270636} {:answer/id #uuid "aa5496f6-fdf1-5cc6-a7ce-dbb55d245952" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270789} {:answer/id #uuid "c681c4dd-1f9e-524b-b441-d45c91ba1047" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271017}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c681c4dd-1f9e-524b-b441-d45c91ba1047" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271017} :answer-field/id #uuid "7ce1772f-fae9-51d4-86d3-256af231e875" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271730}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "bcfaf845-ee85-5f89-a0ff-887be1bdd8e1" :question/math-academy-id "q-141108" :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-y,\\,y(0)=1.\n$$\n\nYou're given that $y=A{e}^{-x}$ is the solution to this initial value problem. What is the value of the constant $A?$" :question/worked-solution "We're given that $y=A{e}^{-x}$ is the solution to the initial value problem. Therefore, it must satisfy the differential equation *and* the initial condition $y(0)=1.$\n\nSubstituting the initial condition $y(0)=1$ into our solution and solving for $A,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =A{e}^{-x} \\\\ 1 & =A{e}^{-0} \\\\ 1 & =A(1) \\\\ A & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny=1{e}^{-x}={e}^{-x}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272213 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "27af5735-67e6-5745-837d-f3e8373eb100" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269619} {:answer/id #uuid "53ea0659-8633-53a6-87c4-5c537b0142b1" :answer/type {:db/ident :